WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.560
Tijuana's downtown is squeaky clean.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:09.090
Its main street is lined with bars, restaurants
and shops.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:16.199
And it sports the unavoidable local absurdity
which serves as a tourist attraction.

00:00:16.199 --> 00:00:20.730
These are the images the city of Tijuana wants
the world to see - in these days more than

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.600
ever.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.560
The reality is very different.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:30.199
Tijuana is sheltering almost three thousand
migrants from Central America – so called

00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:36.180
“Caravan migrants” in the Benito Juarez
sports complex.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:43.519
Now, with the number of migrants we have in
town the situation is under control and manageable.

00:00:43.519 --> 00:00:54.049
We are cooperating and have the support of
the state police and other security agencies.

00:00:54.049 --> 00:00:57.350
They may have control of the situation for
now.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:03.389
But authorities expect that by the end of
the week an additional 900 migrants will have

00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:04.420
arrived.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:09.580
That influx could make conditions worse here,
things could become unmanageable quickly - A

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.430
major concern not only for city officials
and some locals.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:17.420
A worry – shared even by Cindy and her three
sisters.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.810
The women arrived here hours ago.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:23.810
Making their way from Honduras in just over
a month they were separated from other family

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.799
members along the way.

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:29.830
Cindy can’t wait to get out of Tijuana and
into the US.

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:37.579
We are going to ask for asylum in the United
States, because we ran away from our country,

00:01:37.579 --> 00:01:43.149
we are afraid in our country.

00:01:43.149 --> 00:01:49.950
We don’t have work there, but most of all
we are afraid of the violence.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:54.369
Cindy and her sisters know that asking for
asylum in the US is one thing, but that actually

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:58.830
qualifying for and getting it is much harder.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:02.049
Everybody who has a god has hope.

00:02:02.049 --> 00:02:05.479
Hope or not - Others don’t want to take
their chances.

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:09.659
Starting the legal asylum process is not an
option for them.

00:02:09.659 --> 00:02:14.090
I will take the risk and jump the fence.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:18.950
For the last four days another Honduran migrant
has been sheltering in Tijuana.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:22.270
Francisco says he's lost faith in the U.S.
asylum process.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.270
Why?

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:29.760
“I don’t want to ask for asylum, because
I heard that out of a thousand people just

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.250
about 10 get asylum.”

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:39.629
Tijuana– for most of the migrants just a
layover on their journey to their final destination,

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:44.310
the United States of America.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:48.409
This family are here to request asylum.

00:02:48.409 --> 00:02:52.659
Volunteers at the border crossing are helping
them with the application, which can take

00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:55.470
at least two months to process.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:03:01.270
That's a long time to wait without work or
shelter for Aurelio, his wife and four children.

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:07.739
Their journey from Guatemala already took
a month.

00:03:07.739 --> 00:03:11.110
Having to wait here is what worries us.

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:13.450
We can't stay outside for so long.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.910
It's very cold.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:21.640
If Tijuana's government gives us the chance
to work, then we'll stay and see how we can

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.180
get into the US."

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:32.599
The local government has assured migrants
that they CAN work here.

00:03:32.599 --> 00:03:39.920
But some experts doubt the city can support
so many in the long term.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:48.549
There are around 7,000 jobs that could be
offered to both Mexicans and migrants.

00:03:48.549 --> 00:03:54.469
The local manuacturing industry could employ
some, although it currently doesn't have much

00:03:54.469 --> 00:04:01.420
hiring capacity.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:06.469
The NGO that's helped the caravan -- Pueblos
Sin Fronteras -- is keen to point out any

00:04:06.469 --> 00:04:07.469
opportunities.

00:04:07.469 --> 00:04:12.420
The aid workers want to keep the migrants'
spirits high, and convince them of the dangers

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:15.069
of crossing the border illegally.

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:27.890
There are 20,000 jobs in construction that
even offer training to those without experience.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:33.350
More than 500 people could die in a year when
tensions are high, because there's a lot of

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:40.160
violence."

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.070
The NGO is urging migrants to be patient.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:49.110
But the lack of shelter and hostile atmosphere
in Tijuana is fuelling their despair.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:53.760
More and more of them are considering climbing
the wall or even swimming around it.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:58.890
Vladimir is one of them.

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:01.980
We're thinking about crossing by sea.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:08.530
Wait until the waves go down, then take your
chance.

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:14.330
The migrants have little chance of being granted
asylum in the US under the Trump administration

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:19.530
although there's a bit more hope now that
a US court has barred Trump from denying asylum

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:24.670
to those entering illegally.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:31.370
Some families are prepared to risk everything
to try.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:34.970
If they don't let us in through the ports
of entry, we'll have to jump the wall.

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:37.870
There's no other way.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.060
The biggest risk is on the other side.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:46.840
We could get killed, but we have to help each
other cross the barrier.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:51.090
The migrants AREN'T currently considering
jumping the wall en masse.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:57.690
But they're also not ruling out protest action
to demand faster processing of asylum requests.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:01.221
More Central American migrants are still making
their way towards Tijuana.

00:06:01.221 --> 00:06:02.221
The Mexican government has installed metal
barriers at this border crossing for cars,

00:06:02.221 --> 00:06:03.221
in order to stop a potential rush of people.

00:06:03.221 --> 00:06:04.221
Die mexikanische Regierung hat diese Metallzäune
aufgestellt, um die Sicherheit an diesem Grenzübergang

00:06:04.221 --> 00:06:05.221
für Autos angesichts eines möglichen Marsches
von Migranten hierher zu verstärken.

00:06:05.221 --> 00:06:09.750
They face a dilemma: jump the wall or endure
the uncertain wait for asylum.

